Contract and acceptance Record; original stage label **11a** is retained only for requirement/task/workflow IDs. [Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) is the execution authority.

Contributing packages: [Reusable electronic device integration](../features/Electronic-Devices.lingua); [PCB layout, checks and fabrication data](../features/Pcb.lingua); [Electronic definitions and schematics](../features/Schematics.lingua)

## Scheduling interpretation

The linked packages own implementation and its task order. This Record preserves the full source requirements, interface details, examples, research, milestones, fixtures, failure cases and completion evidence. Its `#requires` edges mean all contributors are needed to close this whole contract, not that every consumer waits for this join. Former references to earlier/later stages, delivery cycles or deferred tails describe the appropriate capability subset and composed proofs; they do not restore the removed global sequence. Incomplete unrelated siblings are not regression failures. All already verified affected capabilities must continue working.

For a mixed milestone, each contributor records its verified subset, then this join runs the actual composed workflow when all contributors exist. Do not mark the full milestone done from a local helper or silently drop geographic/hosted/numerical portions. Published exports remain usable without reopening their implementation solely to await this join; fixes to real interface defects remain mandatory.


Finish with a reusable electronic device whose schematic, board layout, 3D assembly and functional behavior share stable identities and one accepted edit path. Its internal design remains editable while ordinary scene use runs a cheap functional model. This stage delivers electronic authoring and design checks; numerical circuit execution begins in stage 15a.

## Required workflow milestones

- [ ] **11a.M01.** Create a hierarchical schematic with declared component pins, nets, supply/reference connections and exposed device ports. Select the same component or pin from schematic, table and scene; edit, undo and reopen without losing identity.
- [ ] **11a.M02.** Realize the bounded design as a two-copper-layer PCB: assign compatible footprints, place components, route traces and plated through vias, and inspect the board in its CAD enclosure. Cross-probe schematic pins, footprint pads, copper connectivity and 3D occurrences.
- [ ] **11a.M03.** Run the declared electrical and board checks, inspect diagnostics by stable selection, repair an intentional open/short/clearance error and export the supported fabrication package with exact source revisions and limits. Passing checks does not claim manufacturing yield or electrical performance.
- [ ] **11a.M04.** Expose the board as a reusable sensor device, choose its stage 07 functional model and use it in the room while internal geometry is unallocated. Reopen the PCB, edit it, inspect stale approximation status, preserve unselected copies and save offline.
- [ ] **11a.M05.** Create the device abstractly first, then associate a detailed implementation through explicit port/model mappings. Share an allowed schematic or coarse device with a restricted visitor without revealing private internals or executing supplied code.

## Entry and scope

- [ ] Follow the [general workflow, acceptance and compression rules](../Workspace-Development.lingua#dependency-driven-delivery-and-repair). Preserve existing requirement IDs. Electronic implementation follows its schematic, PCB and reusable-device package prerequisites; recover only the actual provider handoffs. No whole stage 11 gate is required for schematic work.
- [ ] Build on shared definition/occurrence identity, typed connections, native transactions, purpose-specific representations, exact geometry where required, artifact delivery and policy. Re-audit source ownership before coding. Domain payloads belong in the shared pure model boundary; engine/store accept changes; the native Rust interface owns editors; bounded evaluators own checks/exports. No separate ECAD database, save engine or authority system.
- [ ] Scope the first board explicitly: two copper layers, through vias, simple pads, straight routed segments, a closed board outline and a bounded component library. Native manual placement/routing is required. Autorouting, arbitrary multilayer stackups, flex/rigid-flex, controlled-impedance prediction, firmware execution and advanced fabrication are later separate capabilities. Preserve unsupported imported content and diagnostics rather than silently flattening it.

