## Architecture and task requirements

- [ ] A reusable component separates logical pin roles, schematic appearance, physical package/footprint, purchasing metadata, functional model and optional numerical device model. Matching by display name is insufficient. Explicit mappings validate coverage, terminal kinds, units and revision; unsupported pin mappings block the affected operation while the rest remains inspectable.
- [ ] Schematic, PCB and 3D placement are related representations with different editable data. A board-placement edit changes its accepted placement and dependent geometry; it does not silently rewrite schematic connectivity. An intentional net edit invalidates layout connectivity/check results and shows required repair. Source updates preserve known correspondence and expose deleted/split/ambiguous pads or pins.
- [ ] Enclosures, connectors, mounting holes, board dimensions, component heights and keepouts use the same CAD frames/units and assembly interfaces. Library 3D appearance may be approximate; measurement and manufacturing use only the declared suitable source. Trace shape may later supply resistance/parasitic extraction, but no such prediction follows merely from drawing copper.
- [ ] A module's external contract includes required/optional ports, outputs, initialization and model validity. An electrical supply terminal and the core functional `supply_available` signal remain distinct. Stage 15a supplies the explicit electrical-to-functional adapter; no hidden Boolean-to-voltage conversion is built here.
- [ ] A label such as camera does not generate optics, firmware, protocol or semiconductor physics. Use an implemented behavior template with stated capabilities. A motion-sensor board may initially accept an idealized scene-stimulus input; its mapping is an assumption until a separately validated transducer model replaces it.
- [ ] Native tooling includes schematic canvas, board layers/routing view, component/net table, 3D cross-selection and diagnostics. Keyboard/numeric tools, scope, focus, accessible status and undo follow the existing workspace contracts. Model selection remains in the shared stage 07 inspector, including unsupported/stale status; do not introduce a separate electronics runtime control system.
- [ ] Bound nested modules, connection counts, polygon complexity, library decode sizes, queued checks and exported bytes. Reuse source assets across instances; count unique boards and occurrences separately. Imported executable models remain inert artifacts until a trusted installed evaluator is explicitly admitted at its later stage. Embedded library/dependency licenses and credits accompany the relevant Sand/assets.

## Delivery cycles and retained workflows

- [ ] **Cycle A — Connected design:** T01–T03, actual schematic/native/save path and mapped component identities.
- [ ] **Cycle B — Physical realization:** T04–T06, board/3D/checks/export with independent connectivity and geometric evidence.
- [ ] **Cycle C — Reusable functional device:** T07–T08, source retention, model association, mixed scene, offline and authority recovery.

| Retained workflow | Coverage and delivery | Required evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **11a.W01 — Author and realize a connected board** | Built-in schematic/layout/3D tools; M01/M02, T01–T04. | Stable pin/pad/component mappings, intended nets, native routing/undo/reopen, enclosure units and measured editing/check costs. |
| **11a.W02 — Inspect errors and export a bounded design** | Built-in checks/export plus B43 recipe; M03, T05/T06. | Independently specified opens/shorts/clearances detected, source-keyed diagnostics, supported export independently inspected, stale results cannot pass. |
| **11a.W03 — Reuse a device at different structural detail** | Shared functional models plus sensor-board recipe; M04/M05, T07/T08. | Abstract-first/detailed-first mapping, no dormant numerical execution, unchanged external functional behavior, dependency invalidation, offline closure and disclosure checks. |

## Fixture specifications owned here

- [ ] **B43 — Board and device boundary.** Use a small authored sensor/controller board with explicit supply and output connectors, idealized stimulus input, timer/threshold behavior, switch/driver and indicator load. Freeze a bounded component/model library and a hand-checked expected net graph. Provide a two-layer layout, at least one through via, mounting features and an enclosure using existing geometry. Include a missing connection, deliberately shorted nets, an illegal clearance, a mismatched pad mapping and an unsupported imported feature. The functional sensor contract is inherited from B42; physical transducer accuracy is not claimed.
- [ ] Pin counts, board size, trace/via/polygon counts, decoded bytes, library revisions and export subsets before coding. Measure native selection/routing/commit/check latency, transient old/new buffers and last-demand release on named hardware. Adopt explicit thresholds from the current core profile and the actual B43 workload; do not inherit a synthetic draw benchmark as ECAD performance evidence.

## Concrete acceptance replay

- [ ] **11a.P01 / W01.** Place and connect components natively, assign footprints, route the board, cross-select terminals in all views, move a component, undo and reopen. Compare connectivity against the independent graph, not the evaluator's own serialized output. A camera/appearance change must not change a net or pin mapping.
- [ ] **11a.P02 / W02.** Introduce each specified fault, observe its exact selected diagnostic, repair it, and export. Inspect exported layers/drills/placement with an independent reader/reference; test wrong units, invalid geometry, stale completion and interrupted export. Preserve the previous valid package and never label partial output complete.
- [ ] **11a.P03 / W03.** Place two device occurrences, use one functional sensor to control the B42 lamp, unload PCB detail and continue detection. Reopen the board offline, change one selected instance, expose outdated derived mappings/models and preserve the other instance. Build the same external device abstractly, associate the board explicitly, and share only its permitted projection. Verify no solver, arbitrary code or external equipment action starts.

## Advance gate

- [ ] Pass M01–M05 and W01–W03 through the real native/backend/persistence/permission path. Preserve earlier core workflows, B42 behavior and Stage 11 assembly/takeoff. Record source/build/profile, independent expected results, actual measurements, usability review, denied/stale/failure recovery and remaining unsupported scope.
- [ ] Do not complete this stage with an imported mesh, a schematic screenshot, an external application's window or an evaluator placeholder. Use repository cargo xtask/Nix checks and `cargo check` with warnings as errors during implementation; append-only migration rules apply if storage changes. No implementation is authorized by this plan edit alone.

